==English==

===Pronunciation===
* {{rhymes|ɛə(r)weɪ|lang=en}}

===Noun===
{{en-noun}}

# {{lb|en|golf}} the area between the [[tee]] and the [[green]], where the [[grass]] is cut short
# any [[tract]] of [[land]] free from [[obstacle]]s
# ([[military|Military]]) A channel either from [[offshore]], in a [[river]], or in a [[harbor]] that has enough [[depth]] to accommodate the [[draft]] of large [[vessel]]s.(JP 4-01.6)
# {{lb|en|nautical}} a [[navigable]] [[channel]] in a [[harbour]], [[offshore]] etc; the usual [[course]] taken by [[vessel]]s in such places.
#* '''1899''', Joseph Conrad, ''[[s:Heart of Darkness|Heart of Darkness]]'', [[s:Heart of Darkness/Section I|section 1]]
#*: Lights of ships moved in the '''fairway'''—a great stir of lights going up and going down.

